HL7 FHIR R4 core package (crates/fhir/fixtures/r4)
  Derived from hl7.fhir.r4.core 4.0.1 by crates/fhir/generate-r4.py, which keeps the
  StructureDefinition, SearchParameter, CodeSystem, ValueSet and ConceptMap resources.
  HL7 International publishes the package under CC0-1.0, as its package.json declares.
  https://hl7.org/fhir/

Prepared FHIR packages (refhir-packages.bundle, in release archives and container images)
  Made by `refhir package-bundle` when a release is built, from hl7.fhir.r4.core 4.0.1,
  hl7.fhir.uv.sdc 4.0.0 and the packages they depend on (hl7.terminology.r4 7.1.0,
  hl7.fhir.uv.extensions.r4 5.3.0-ballot-tc1, hl7.fhir.uv.tools.r4 1.1.2 and
  hl7.fhir.uv.xver-r5.r4 0.1.0): the StructureDefinition, SearchParameter, CodeSystem, ValueSet,
  ConceptMap and CompartmentDefinition resources they hold, and the value set expansions worked
  out from them. HL7 International publishes each package under CC0-1.0, as its package.json
  declares. https://hl7.org/fhir/

International Patient Summary package (crates/fhir/fixtures/ips)
  hl7.fhir.uv.ips 2.0.1, as the FHIR package registry serves it, unchanged. The IPS tests install it
  and check HL7's own example summaries against its profiles. HL7 International publishes the
  package under CC0-1.0, as its package.json declares. https://hl7.org/fhir/uv/ips/

Other test packages (crates/fhir/fixtures/*)
  The remaining directories are small packages written for the test suites. Several are
  named after HL7 packages (hl7.fhir.uv.sdc, hl7.fhir.uv.extensions.r4, hl7.terminology.r4,
  and others) and are slices or imitations of them, not complete copies. Each has a
  package.json naming it.

FHIRPath test suite (crates/fhirpath/tests/hl7/)
  tests-fhir-r4.xml and its input resources are the FHIRPath test suite that HL7 maintains
  in https://github.com/FHIR/fhir-test-cases (Apache License 2.0).

